Z||000000||Carolina 88GT||02-23-2000||06:06 PM||||ARRGGGHHHHH!  Damn Farmers!  comming home from work...got behind scooby do's van pulling a utility wagon.  Something told me I should have passed em....but NOOOO....damn gate on the utility wagon was held closed by a tire iron and a metal spike.  Metal spike bounced out doing 55mph...hit the road...bounced 20 feet into the air..proceded to bounce off my front left headlight (forntunately it was closed) and skim down the left part of my rear clip.  Fortunately it didnt break the sail panel, however, it punctured the front bumper about 1/2 inch long, cracked the top part of the headlight cover and put an inch long gash in my rear clip!  I know I was planning on painting my car....but didnt plan on it so soon.  guess my weekend is going to be spent filling and wet sanding.||||reg||8
